          "evidence_id": "sfev-fc648fbc19e8ff51",
          "evidence_type": "inquiry_or_scientific_method",
          "paraphrase": "The scientists systematically test many solvents on the fragment, none of which affect it.",
          "provenance": [
            {
              "backend": "anthropic",
              "normalization_notes": [
                "used bounded whitespace/typography/case fallback"
              ],
              "raw_id": "ev05",
              "source": "model",
              "source_chunk_id": null
            }
          ],
          "quote": "There were ammonia and caustic soda, alcohol and ether, nauseous carbon disulphide and a dozen others; but although the weight grew steadily less as time passed, and the fragment seemed to be slightly cooling, there was no change in the solvents to show that they had attacked the substance at all."
